#!/usr/bin/env python3
# tools/ops/medium_tier_diagnosis.py
#
# The MEDIUM-tier diagnosis, session 2 (docs/medium-tier-diagnosis-brief-2026-09-16.md section 3, questions D-1 to D-12;
# read: docs/medium-tier-diagnosis-read-2026-09-17.md). Python 3 standard library only (no numpy).
#
# Inputs (gitignored, regenerated by the instrument):
#   <cache>/diagnosis-rows.csv          SwingFallbackRead --mode diagexport: one line per swing read population row,
#                                        the candle-walk outcomes (main window, carried 24 h), the half, logged context.
#   <cache>/rescore-attribution.csv     SwingFallbackRead --mode rescore: per-vote signed points per row (session 1).
#   settings.json (tracked, read-only)  verdict percentages and nominal penalty and bonus magnitudes.
#   <cache>/rescore-eras/settings-v*.json  (optional) proves those values are identical in every era.
#
# Rules fixed before the first run (brief section 4 discipline):
#   * Population: the swing read population (8,810 rows). Sessions separate, never pooled for outcomes.
#   * Outcome: net EV per trade, bps, maker/maker, main window primary, carried 24 h secondary. Success = target hit.
#   * Tier: the logged verdict tier. Scores: the LOGGED scores (diagnosis-rows). Votes: the re-scored breakdown
#     (attribution); rows whose re-score does not match all six fields are kept and counted (sensitivity: excluded).
#   * Vote lean for the trade side X and the other side Y: points(X) - points(Y). Agree > 0, oppose < 0, absent = 0.
#   * Halves: the stability read's split (first floor(D/2) UTC trading days), carried in the export.
#   * CI: 95 % percentile bootstrap of whole UTC trading days, fixed seed, --resamples (default 10,000).
#   * Readable: n >= 100 in every cell a statistic uses, else NOT READABLE.
#   * Label for a comparison d, first match wins (the census rule):
#       NOT READABLE (FULL n < 100 in a cell) -> CONFIRMED (both halves readable, both CIs exclude 0, same sign)
#       -> H1 FINDING, H2 SAME SIGN NOT SIGNIFICANT -> H1 FINDING, H2 CONTRADICTS OR NOT READABLE
#       -> DISCOVERY ONLY (H2) -> NO DIFFERENCE SHOWN.
#   * A cause counts as CONFIRMED only with the CONFIRMED label. Everything else is DISCOVERY ONLY or no finding.
#   * D-1 monotone: OLS slope of per-row net EV on the effective score share (per 0.1 of regime max) and on the
#     effective margin (per point). Monotone increasing = slope > 0 CONFIRMED.
#   * D-3 anti-predictive vote: d = EV(agree) - EV(oppose) < 0 CONFIRMED. Also reported within tier (weights = the
#     tier's agree + oppose rows in each resample).
#   * D-4 tier crossing: counterfactual effective score = effective - applied delta of that mutation on the trade side.
#     Applied delta = the label's points where the label carries only that mutation on that side, else the nominal
#     magnitude (named per mutation). Ka: crossed rows vs untouched rows of the landing tier. Kb: crossed rows vs
#     untouched rows of the origin tier.
#   * D-7 re-weighting: MEDIUM post-stratified to WEAK's stratum mix over strata where both tiers have rows.
#   * D-8 extension terciles: cut points from the session's H1 rows (all tiers), then applied to every row.
#   * D-9 episode: same-side population signals, each within the session's main window of the previous one.
#   * D-12 era segments per session at the scoring edges that touch it; H1/H2 is not used there.
#
# Run (from the repo root):
#   dotnet build tools/ops/SwingFallbackRead/SwingFallbackRead.vbproj -c Release
#   dotnet tools/ops/SwingFallbackRead/bin/Release/net8.0/SwingFallbackRead.dll --root . --mode rescore \
#     --fetch aws_fetch/20260913-153704 --pooled AWS-copybacks/pooled-book-2026-09-09/analysis_log_pooled.csv
#   dotnet tools/ops/SwingFallbackRead/bin/Release/net8.0/SwingFallbackRead.dll --root . --mode diagexport \
#     --fetch aws_fetch/20260913-153704 --pooled AWS-copybacks/pooled-book-2026-09-09/analysis_log_pooled.csv
#   python tools/ops/medium_tier_diagnosis.py --root .

